    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"7.1.Goodness-of-fit tests\"\nsubtitle: \"The binomial test\"\nauthor: \"Bárbara D. Bitarello\"\ndate: \"11-19-2025\"\nkeywords: \"Goodness-of-fit tests\"\nformat:\n  revealjs:\n    hash-type: number\n    embed-resources: false\n    smaller: true\n    scrollable: false\n    incremental: true\n    slide-number: true\n    transition: slide\n    background-transition: fade\n    highlight-style: ayu-dark\n    footer: \"B215: Biostatistics with R\"\n    center-title-slide: false\n    theme: [custom.scss]\n    callout-appearance: simple\n    code-fold: true\n    chalkboard: true\n    auto-slide: 133000\ncode-link: true\nexecute:\n  echo: false\n  freeze: auto\nknitr: \n  opts_chunk:\n    tidy: true\n    tidy-opts: { \"value\": \"list(width.cutoff = I(60))\", \"tag\": \"!expr\" }\neditor: \n  markdown: \n    wrap: 72\n---\n\n\n\n## Outline\n\n•Goodness-of-fit tests\n\n•The proportional model\n\n•The $\\chi^2$ distribution\n\n•Degrees of freedom\n\n•The $\\chi^2$ test\n\n•Using $\\chi^2$ to test if data are distributed according to a poisson\ndistribution\n\n## Goodness of Fit Tests\n\n::: r-fit-text\n<font size = 7>Does <font color = \"#E69F00\">data</font> come from a\n<font color = \"#56B4E9\">given distribution</font> with specified\n<font color = \"#56B4E9\">parameters</font>?</font>\n:::\n\n## NHL player birth months 🏒\n\n::: goal\n**Biological hypothesis**: Being born earlier in the year makes players\nstand out when young, helping them achieve later success.\n:::\n\n::::: columns\n::: {.column width=\"35%\"}\n$H_0$: Elite hockey players are born randomly across the year.\n\n$H_A$: Elite hockey players are NOT born randomly across the year.\n:::\n\n::: {.column width=\"\\\"65%\"}\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](GoodnessOfFit_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-1-1.png){width=480}\n:::\n:::\n\n:::\n:::::\n\n## Testing!\n\n::::: columns\n::: {.column width=\"30%\"}\n$H_0$: Prop birth months of NHLers is like that of other humans.\n\n$H_A$: Prop birth months of NHLers is unlike that of other humans.\n:::\n\n::: {.column width=\"70%\"}\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table\" style=\"font-size: 20px; width: auto !important; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n<caption style=\"font-size: initial !important;\">Human  births by month</caption>\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> month </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> births (%) </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Jan </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.94 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Feb </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.63 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Mar </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.72 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> April </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.63 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> May </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.95 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> June </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.57 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Jul </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.76 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Aug </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.50 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Sept </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.54 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Oct </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.19 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Nov </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.70 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Dec </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.87 </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n:::\n:::::\n\n::: aside\nVentura et al. (2001). Births: final data for 1999. National Vital\nStatistics Reports Vol. 49, No. 1.\n:::\n\n## Introducing $\\chi^2$\n\n$\\chi^2$ summarizes the fit of **categorical** data to expectations.\n\n\n\n![](images/clipboard-1606444611.png){fig-alt=\"shows chi-squared formula with annotations: O=observed, E=expected, chi-squared (greek symbol)\"\nfig-align=\"center\"}\n\n$\\chi^2 = 0$: Data perfectly match null hypothesis expectations\n\n$χ^2 > 0$: Data show deviation from null hypothesis expectations\n\n## Finding Expectations\n\n::::: columns\n::: column\nExpected number of births in month $i$ is:\n\n$E[X] = n_{total} × \\text{Null proportion}$\n\n$n_{total} = 1245$ (just add up the births column)\n\n$$E[X_i] = n_{total} \\times \\text{expected propotion}_i$$\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nnhl |>\n    mutate(expected.prop = c(0.0794, 0.0763, 0.0872, 0.0863, 0.0895, 0.0857, 0.0876,\n        0.085, 0.0854, 0.0819, 0.077, 0.0787)) |>\n    mutate(expected.n = expected.prop * sum(births), `expected %` = 100 * expected.prop)\n```\n:::\n\n:::\n\n::: column\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table\" style=\"font-size: 18px; width: auto !important; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> month </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> births </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> expected % </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> expected.n </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Jan </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 133 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.94 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 98.8 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Feb </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 125 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.63 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 95.0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Mar </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 114 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.72 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 108.6 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Apr </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 119 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.63 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 107.4 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> May </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 119 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.95 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 111.4 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> June </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 123 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.57 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 106.7 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Jul </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 96 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.76 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 109.1 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Aug </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 91 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.50 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 105.8 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Sep </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 83 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.54 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 106.3 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Oct </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 84 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.19 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 102.0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Nov </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 73 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.70 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 95.9 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Dec </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 85 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.87 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 98.0 </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n:::\n:::::\n\n## Finding $\\chi^2$ \\[1/2\\]\n\n::::: columns\n::: column\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table\" style=\"font-size: 18px; width: auto !important; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> month </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> births </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> expected % </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> expected.n </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Jan </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 133 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.94 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 98.8 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Feb </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 125 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.63 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 95.0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Mar </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 114 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.72 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 108.6 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Apr </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 119 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.63 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 107.4 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> May </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 119 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.95 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 111.4 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> June </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 123 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.57 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 106.7 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Jul </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 96 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.76 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 109.1 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Aug </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 91 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.50 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 105.8 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Sep </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 83 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.54 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 106.3 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Oct </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 84 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.19 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 102.0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Nov </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 73 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.70 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 95.9 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Dec </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 85 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.87 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 98.0 </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n:::\n\n::: column\nExample: January\n\n$E=98.9$\n\n$O=133$\n\n$\\frac{(O_{i}-E_{i})^2}{E_{i}}=?$\n\n$\\frac{(133-98.9)^2}{98.9}=\\frac{1162.81}{98.9}=11.76$\n:::\n:::::\n\n## Finding $\\chi^2$ \\[2/2\\]\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nnhl |>\n    mutate(sq_dev_over_expect = (expected.n - births)^2/expected.n)\n```\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table\" style=\"font-size: 18px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> month </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> month.num </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> births </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> expected.prop </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> expected.n </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> expected % </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> sq_dev_over_expect </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Jan </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 133 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.079 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 98.9 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.94 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 11.795 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Feb </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 2 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 125 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.076 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 95.0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.63 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 9.478 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Mar </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 3 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 114 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.087 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 108.6 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.72 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.272 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Apr </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 4 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 119 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.086 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 107.4 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.63 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.243 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> May </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 5 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 119 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.090 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 111.4 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.95 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.515 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> June </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 6 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 123 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.086 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 106.7 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.57 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 2.491 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Jul </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 96 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.088 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 109.1 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.76 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.564 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Aug </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 91 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.085 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 105.8 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.50 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 2.077 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Sep </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 9 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 83 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.085 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 106.3 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.54 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 5.116 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Oct </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 10 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 84 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.082 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 102.0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8.19 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 3.165 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Nov </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 11 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 73 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.077 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 95.9 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.70 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 5.454 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Dec </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 12 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 85 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0.079 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 98.0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7.87 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.720 </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n\nNow find $\\chi^2$ by summing over all\n$\\frac{(\\text{O}_i - \\text{E}_i)^2}{\\text{E}_i}$\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nobs.chi2 <- nhl |>\n    summarise(chi2 = sum(sq_dev_over_expect))\nobs.chi2\n## # A tibble: 1 × 1\n##    chi2\n##   <dbl>\n## 1  44.9\n```\n:::\n\n\n<font size = 10>\n$\\chi^2 = 44.89$</font>\n\n## From Test Stat to P-value \\[1/2\\]\n\n\n\n::: columns\n\n::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n***By simulation***\n\n• Randomly assign hockey players birth dates. $\\chi^2$ \n\n• Calculate $\\chi^2$ for these random data following the null. \n\n:::\n\n::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n• Repeat this many times. \n\n• Compare observed to generated under the null.\n\n:::\n\n:::\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](GoodnessOfFit_files/figure-revealjs/chi2-1.png){fig-align='center' width=960}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## From Test Stat to P-value \\[2/2\\]\n\nThe $\\chi^2$ distribution describes expected values of $\\chi^2$ under\n$H_0$.\\\nThe p-value is the area under the upper tail of the distribution.\\\nYou can see solid agreement between our simulations and the $\\chi^2$\ndistribution. We often use the $\\chi^2$ for testing comparing\ncategorical counts to expectations.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](GoodnessOfFit_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-6-1.png){width=960}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n# WHY DOES THIS WORK? {.dark-theme}\n\nTHE $\\chi^2$ DISTRIBUTION’S\n\nPROPERTIES\n\n## Introduction to $\\chi^2$ distribution\n\n• The $\\chi^2$ distribution describes the sampling distribution of\n$\\chi^2$ under a null hypothesis predicting expected categorical counts.\n\n• There are many $\\chi^2$ distributions, each associated with a\ndifferent number of degrees of freedom. \n\n• The $\\chi^2$ distributions are\ncontinuous probability distributions, so we use the *area under the\ncurve* (not the height of the curve) to obtain an **APPROXIMATE** P-value. NOTE: This is a one-tailed test!\n\n## Introduction to $\\chi^2$ distribution\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](GoodnessOfFit_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-7-1.png){width=960}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## What Is A Degree of Freedom?\n\n<font size = 7> For $\\chi^2$ tests,</font>\\\ndf = \\# categories - 1 - \\# params estimated from data\n\n<font size = 7> More broadly... </font>\\\nHow many data points can \"wobble around\" following initial estimation of\nyour model.\n\nE.g. $s^2=\\frac{\\sum (x-\\bar x)^2}{n-1}; n=10$\n\n• First we calculate the mean and then we need to calculate each\n$(x−\\bar x)^2$ for each data point.\n\n• But note that only $n−1$ data points are truly free to have *any*\nvalue. I.e., if you know the value $x$ for 9 of your 10 data points, the\nlast one can be inferred. So this statistic has $n− 1$ degrees of\nfreedom.\n\n## Assumptions of $\\chi^2$ tests\n\n-   No expected values $< 1$\\\n-   No more than $20\\%$ of expected values $< 5.$\n\n. . .\n\nDo we meet these?\n\n. . .\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table\" style=\"font-size: 20px; width: auto !important; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> month </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Jan </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Feb </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Mar </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Apr </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> May </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> June </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Jul </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Aug </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Sep </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Oct </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Nov </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Dec </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> expected.n </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 99 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 95 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 109 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 107 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 111 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 107 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 109 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 106 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 106 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 102 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 96 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 98 </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## $\\chi^2$ P-Value and Stats Tables\n\n<font color = #6C8645>**Statistical Table A**</font> in your book \\[old\nfashioned, for  exam\\].\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table\" style=\"\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;color: lightgrey !important;background-color: black !important;\"> df | a </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;color: lightgrey !important;background-color: black !important;\"> 0.1 </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;color: lightgrey !important;background-color: black !important;\"> 0.05 </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;color: lightgrey !important;background-color: black !important;\"> 10^-2 </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;color: lightgrey !important;background-color: black !important;\"> 10^-3 </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;color: lightgrey !importa